'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '{\\n  \"kind\": \"callout\",\\n  \"tone\": \"warning\",\\n  \"title\": \"Is the soil the plant\\'s food?\",\\n  \"body\": \"On the windowsill, the plant sits in soil, and its roots are buried in it. It is tempting to say the plant\\'s food is the soil, pulled up through those roots. But look again: a plant is a producer, a living thing that makes its own food inside itself. The soil is only one of its intakes \\\\u2014 taken in through the roots alongside water \\\\u2014 not the food itself. So if you catch yourself reading the soil as the plant\\'s meal, check the reading: the plant still makes the food, and the soil is only a supply. Before you move on, tell yourself which reading fits the plant: the soil as its food, or the plant as the maker of its own food?\"}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '1 validation error:\\n```json\\n[\\n  {\\n    \"type\": \"missing\",\\n    \"loc\": [\\n      \"response\"\\n    ],\\n    \"msg\": \"Field required\"\\n  }\\n]\\n```\\n\\nFix the errors and try again.'}], 'model': 'deepseek-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 8000, 'stream': False}, 'extra_json': {'thinking': {'type': 'disabled'}}}"}
