akes in through its roots from what it makes. The contrast section puts the producer idea against the soil-as-food and water-as-food readings on the same plant so the boundary is visible, and the close checks whether the learner now recognizes the plant, not the soil or the water, as the maker of the food.\"\\n    },\\n    \"neighbours\": [\\n      {\\n        \"kind\": \"callout\",\\n        \"reason\": \"Ask the learner to select which reading of the windowsill plant matches the producer idea, surfacing any remaining soil-as-food model.\",\\n        \"role\": \"practice-cue\",\\n        \"teaching_block_id\": \"contrast-b1\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"kind\": \"paragraph\",\\n        \"reason\": \"Set the water-as-food reading against the target on the same windowsill plant and cup of water already in view.\",\\n        \"role\": \"misconception\",\\n        \"teaching_block_id\": \"contrast-b2\"\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \"objective\": \"Recognize that plants are producers that make their own food\",\\n    \"reason\": \"Close with one recognition check asking where the plant\\'s food comes from and whether the plant is a producer.\",\\n    \"role\": \"check\",\\n    \"stage\": \"document_writing\",\\n    \"teaching_block\": {\\n      \"brief\": \"Pose one check that asks the learner to apply the producer idea to the windowsill plant: given that the plant has soil around its roots and water poured in, decide where the plant\\'s food comes from and confirm that the plant is the thing that makes it. Keep the check to this single recognition of the plant as producer, and do not re-explain soil or water as intakes.\",\\n      \"evidence\": \"The objective is a recognition claim about which category the plant belongs to, so the close must read whether the learner places food-making in the plant rather than in the soil or water \\\\u2014 exactly the correct-versus-incorrect signal check-understanding is for.\",\\n      \"id\": \"check-b1\",\\n      \"intent\": \"check-understanding\"\\n    },\\n    \"terminology\": []\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nReturn JSON only for this capability payload.'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Return only valid JSON matching this schema.\\nDo not call tools.\\n{\"properties\": {\"response\": {\"additionalProperties\": true, \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"required\": [\"response\"], \"type\": \"object\", \"title\": \"dict\"}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Return JSON only for the selected capability payload.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '{\\n  \"kind\": \"callout\",\\n  \"tone\": \"important\",\\n  \"title\": \"Check: Where Does the Windowsill Plant\\'s Food Come From?\",\\n  \"body\": \"Look back at the classroom plant on the windowsill. It is growing in soil, and water has been poured into the pot around its roots. Now use the producer idea to decide: where does the food this plant needs actually come from?\\\\n\\\\nDecide, then write one sentence giving your answer. Name the thing that makes the food, and confirm whether that thing is the plant itself. Remember: you are being asked only about which thing makes the food \u2014 you are not being asked to describe how soil or water are taken in.\"\\n}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '1 validation error:\\n```json\\n[\\n  {\\n    \"type\": \"missing\",\\n    \"loc\": [\\n      \"response\"\\n    ],\\n    \"msg\": \"Field required\"\\n  }\\n]\\n```\\n\\nFix the errors and try again.'}], 'model': 'deepseek-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 8000, 'stream': False}, 'extra_json': {'thinking': {'type': 'disabled'}}}"}
