{"timestamp": "2026-09-13T20:56:42.404920+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "openai._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-20289c34-f623-4e4d-ac4b-aa2357d5b0f8', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You author one already-selected educational capability. Follow the\\nsupplied AuthoringDefinition and exact output schema. Preserve block identity, objective, scope,\\nlearner action, source ownership and assessment mode. Do not select another capability or redesign\\nthe teaching plan.\\n\\nPlanning instructions are not final content. For an activity, produce a meaningful prompt, task\\ndata, justified answer relationships and useful feedback as required by the contract. Do not infer\\ncorrectness from option positions, number/word positions, example ordering or arbitrary defaults.\\nDo not copy illustrative examples as unrelated lesson content.\\n\\nTreat approved items as authoritative content. Conversion must preserve their question and answer\\nmeaning. Report incompatibility through the defined error path instead of guessing. Use supported\\nteacher-review only when the work order policy permits it.\\n\\nReturn exactly the selected output schema. Do not emit sibling schemas, markdown wrappers, internal\\nplanning metadata or extra fields. If required information is absent, use the configured\\nmissing-input mechanism; do not create placeholder content to satisfy structure.\\n\\nDo not invent or overwrite knowledge/assessment policy fields. Effective policy is code-owned.\\n\\n## KNOWLEDGE POLICY\\nKnowledge policy: supplied_preferred. Use supplied facts as the primary basis; you may add relevant model knowledge within the objective and constraints. Do not describe model knowledge as approved factual material.\\n\\n## PACKAGE CAPABILITY INSTRUCTIONS\\nCapability: choice.\\r\\n\\r\\nAuthor a complete activity envelope: student-facing prompt, choice config, and feedback.\\r\\n\\r\\n- Write the prompt as a clear question the learner reads directly. The planning brief is context only \u2014 do not copy it verbatim.\\r\\n- Provide feedback.correct and feedback.incorrect messages tied to the question and distractors.\\r\\n- Put options and the correct option id in config.\\r\\n\\r\\n- Use at least two options with unique stable ids.\\r\\n- Exactly one option is correct.\\r\\n- Distractors must be plausible and tied to a stateable misconception.\\r\\n- Do not use this for questions with several defensible answers.\\n\\n## AUTHORING DEFINITION\\n{\\n  \"assessment\": {\\n    \"default\": \"automatic_required\",\\n    \"supported\": [\\n      \"automatic_required\"\\n    ],\\n    \"teacher_review_permitted\": false\\n  },\\n  \"capability_id\": \"choice\",\\n  \"converter_ref\": \"learn.choice.approved_item_converter\",\\n  \"definition_hash\": \"9c9eca46dacb6c6603192a541ee7c019236a8ab713137ae9027d3e3557c1c7eb\",\\n  \"instructions\": \"Capability: choice.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAuthor a complete activity envelope: student-facing prompt, choice config, and feedback.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Write the prompt as a clear question the learner reads directly. The planning brief is context only \\\\u2014 do not copy it verbatim.\\\\r\\\\n- Provide feedback.correct and feedback.incorrect messages tied to the question and distractors.\\\\r\\\\n- Put options and the correct option id in config.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Use at least two options with unique stable ids.\\\\r\\\\n- Exactly one option is correct.\\\\r\\\\n- Distractors must be plausible and tied to a stateable misconception.\\\\r\\\\n- Do not use this for questions with several defensible answers.\",\\n  \"knowledge\": {\\n    \"default\": \"supplied_preferred\",\\n    \"supported\": [\\n      \"supplied_only\",\\n      \"supplied_preferred\",\\n      \"objective_development\"\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \"modes\": [\\n    \"generate\",\\n    \"convert-approved\"\\n  ],\\n  \"native_path\": \"learn\",\\n  \"payload_schema\": {\\n    \"additionalProperties\": true,\\n    \"properties\": {\\n      \"config\": {\\n        \"$id\": \"learn/choice/config.v1\",\\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\\n        \"properties\": {\\n          \"correct_option_id\": {\\n            \"minLength\": 1,\\n            \"type\": \"string\"\\n          },\\n          \"options\": {\\n            \"items\": {\\n              \"additionalProperties\": false,\\n              \"properties\": {\\n                \"explanation\": {\\n                  \"type\": \"string\"\\n                },\\n                \"id\": {\\n                  \"minLength\": 1,\\n                  \"type\": \"string\"\\n                },\\n                \"text\": {\\n                  \"minLength\": 1,\\n                  \"type\": \"string\"\\n                }\\n              },\\n              \"required\": [\\n                \"id\",\\n                \"text\"\\n              ],\\n              \"type\": \"object\"\\n            },\\n            \"minItems\": 2,\\n            \"type\": \"array\",\\n            \"uniqueItems\": true\\n          },\\n          \"presentation\": {\\n            \"enum\": [\\n              \"text\",\\n              \"image\"\\n            ]\\n          }\\n        },\\n        \"required\": [\\n          \"options\",\\n          \"correct_option_id\"\\n        ],\\n        \"type\": \"object\"\\n      },\\n      \"feedback\": {\\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\\n        \"properties\": {\\n          \"correct\": {\\n            \"type\": \"string\"\\n          },\\n          \"incorrect\": {\\n            \"type\": \"string\"\\n          },\\n          \"partial\": {\\n            \"type\": \"string\"\\n          }\\n        },\\n        \"required\": [\\n          \"correct\",\\n          \"incorrect\"\\n        ],\\n        \"type\": \"object\"\\n      },\\n      \"prompt\": {\\n        \"minLength\": 1,\\n        \"type\": \"string\"\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \"required\": [\\n      \"prompt\",\\n      \"config\",\\n      \"feedback\"\\n    ],\\n    \"type\": \"object\"\\n  },\\n  \"required_inputs\": [\\n    \"teaching_plan_block\",\\n    \"learn_selection_decision\",\\n    \"lesson_context\",\\n    \"allowed_facts\",\\n    \"terminology\",\\n    \"learner_action\",\\n    \"approved_items_when_converting\"\\n  ],\\n  \"validator_refs\": [\\n    \"learn.payload_schema\",\\n    \"learn.evaluateChoice\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n\\n## SCOPED REQUEST\\n{\\n  \"inputs\": {\\n    \"allowed_facts\": [\\n      \"plants have roots, stems and leaves\",\\n      \"living things need food to grow\",\\n      \"Plants are living things that can produce their own food\",\\n      \"Plants are called producers\",\\n      \"Use one concrete classroom example.\",\\n      \"Explain that plants make their own food (are producers)\",\\n      \"Identify leaves as the site of photosynthesis and chlorophyll as the light-capturing substance\",\\n      \"Describe photosynthesis as using light, carbon dioxide, and water to produce food and oxygen\",\\n      \"Explain why light is essential for photosynthesis\"\\n    ],\\n    \"approved_items_when_converting\": [],\\n    \"learn_selection_decision\": {\\n      \"capability_id\": \"choice\",\\n      \"lane\": \"interaction\",\\n      \"support_level\": null\\n    },\\n    \"learner_action\": \"select-one\",\\n    \"lesson_context\": {\\n      \"input_availability\": \"supplied_statements\",\\n      \"objective\": \"Recognize that plants are producers that make their own food\",\\n      \"subject\": \"Science\",\\n      \"teaching_plan_revision\": 1,\\n      \"title\": \"The lesson opens on the classroom plant on the windowsill beside the cup of water and asks learners to commit to a guess about where its food comes from, so a personal wrong model is on the table. The explanation then fixes the category term \\\\u2014 the plant is a producer, a living thing that makes its own food \\\\u2014 and separates what the plant takes in through its roots from what it makes. The contrast section puts the producer idea against the soil-as-food and water-as-food readings on the same plant so the boundary is visible, and the close checks whether the learner now recognizes the plant, not the soil or the water, as the maker of the food.\"\\n    },\\n    \"teaching_plan_block\": {\\n      \"action\": \"select-one\",\\n      \"block_id\": \"orient-b1\",\\n      \"brief\": \"Present the concrete case: a potted classroom plant on the windowsill, sitting next to a cup of water. Ask learners where they think the plant\\'s food comes from and have them commit to one answer before anything is explained. Do not name soil, water, or sunlight as food, and do not state the target idea that the plant makes its own food.\",\\n      \"evidence\": \"The objective\\'s recognition claim only becomes meaningful if the learner first holds the concrete windowsill plant and a personal guess to revise, and this is the only place the anchor can be introduced.\",\\n      \"intent\": \"orient\",\\n      \"section_id\": \"orient\"\\n    },\\n    \"terminology\": []\\n  },\\n  \"mode\": \"generate\",\\n  \"resolved_policy\": {\\n    \"assessment_policy_source\": \"package:1.0.0\",\\n    \"definition_hash\": \"9c9eca46dacb6c6603192a541ee7c019236a8ab713137ae9027d3e3557c1c7eb\",\\n    \"definition_version\": \"2.0.0\",\\n    \"effective_assessment_policy\": \"automatic_required\",\\n    \"effective_knowledge_policy\": \"supplied_preferred\",\\n    \"executed_evaluation_mode\": \"accepted-answers\",\\n    \"executed_knowledge_mode\": \"supplied_facts\",\\n    \"fallback_reason\": null,\\n    \"input_availability\": \"supplied_statements\",\\n    \"input_revision\": null,\\n    \"knowledge_policy_source\": \"package:1.0.0\",\\n    \"policy_version\": \"1.0.0\",\\n    \"requested_assessment_policy\": null,\\n    \"requested_knowledge_policy\": null,\\n    \"teacher_review_permitted\": false\\n  },\\n  \"scoped_request\": {\\n    \"action\": \"select-one\",\\n    \"allowed_facts\": [\\n      \"plants have roots, stems and leaves\",\\n      \"living things need food to grow\",\\n      \"Plants are living things that can produce their own food\",\\n      \"Plants are called producers\",\\n      \"Use one concrete classroom example.\",\\n      \"Explain that plants make their own food (are producers)\",\\n      \"Identify leaves as the site of photosynthesis and chlorophyll as the light-capturing substance\",\\n      \"Describe photosynthesis as using light, carbon dioxide, and water to produce food and oxygen\",\\n      \"Explain why light is essential for photosynthesis\"\\n    ],\\n    \"authoring_definition\": {\\n      \"assessment\": {\\n        \"default\": \"automatic_required\",\\n        \"supported\": [\\n          \"automatic_required\"\\n        ],\\n        \"teacher_review_permitted\": false\\n      },\\n      \"asset_requirements\": null,\\n      \"capability_id\": \"choice\",\\n      \"capacity\": {\\n        \"optionMaxWords\": 20,\\n        \"optionsMax\": 5,\\n        \"optionsMin\": 2,\\n        \"stemMaxWords\": 40\\n      },\\n      \"config_schema\": {\\n        \"$id\": \"learn/choice/config.v1\",\\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\\n        \"properties\": {\\n          \"correct_option_id\": {\\n            \"minLength\": 1,\\n            \"type\": \"string\"\\n          },\\n          \"options\": {\\n            \"items\": {\\n              \"additionalProperties\": false,\\n              \"properties\": {\\n                \"explanation\": {\\n                  \"type\": \"string\"\\n                },\\n                \"id\": {\\n                  \"minLength\": 1,\\n                  \"type\": \"string\"\\n                },\\n                \"text\": {\\n                  \"minLength\": 1,\\n                  \"type\": \"string\"\\n                }\\n              },\\n              \"required\": [\\n                \"id\",\\n                \"text\"\\n              ],\\n              \"type\": \"object\"\\n            },\\n            \"minItems\": 2,\\n            \"type\": \"array\",\\n            \"uniqueItems\": true\\n          },\\n          \"presentation\": {\\n            \"enum\": [\\n              \"text\",\\n              \"image\"\\n            ]\\n          }\\n        },\\n        \"required\": [\\n          \"options\",\\n          \"correct_option_id\"\\n        ],\\n        \"type\": \"object\"\\n      },\\n      \"converter_ref\": \"learn.choice.approved_item_converter\",\\n      \"definition_hash\": \"9c9eca46dacb6c6603192a541ee7c019236a8ab713137ae9027d3e3557c1c7eb\",\\n      \"definition_version\": \"2.0.0\",\\n      \"examples\": [\\n        {\\n          \"correct_option_id\": \"air\",\\n          \"options\": [\\n            {\\n              \"explanation\": \"Mass is not drawn from soil.\",\\n              \"id\": \"soil\",\\n              \"text\": \"From the soil\"\\n            },\\n            {\\n              \"id\": \"air\",\\n              \"text\": \"From carbon dioxide in the air\"\\n            },\\n            {\\n              \"explanation\": \"Light supplies energy, not mass.\",\\n              \"id\": \"light\",\\n              \"text\": \"From sunlight alone\"\\n            }\\n          ]\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"field_guidance\": {\\n        \"config.correct_option_id\": \"Must equal the id of exactly one declared option.\",\\n        \"config.options\": \"Stable ids, parallel grammatical form. Give each wrong option an explanation naming the misconception it reveals.\",\\n        \"config.presentation\": \"\\'image\\' renders options as pictures; evaluation is identical, so do not author a separate kind for it.\",\\n        \"feedback.correct\": \"Short message shown when the learner answer is fully correct.\",\\n    